  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Stichting Project Maroon Women Against Gender-Based Violence</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project &apos;Maroon Women Against Gender-Based Violence: Training Peer Educators in Brokopondo&apos; led by Projekta, aims to combat domestic and gender-based violence in Maroon (tribal) communities in rural Suriname. The project will train 15 female community leaders to raise awareness, recognise and respond to GBV. These leaders will then provide training courses to 750 community members. Throughout the project, data will be collected to compile a report on GBV trends in Maroon communities, which will be presented to policymakers upon the project&#x2019;s culmination.</narrative>
  </description>
